  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-performing configs (018, 024) both use pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, but no learned RNA representation (scVI, scGPT) has been tested yet. Multiprofile + avgpool + multimodal + concat is strongly supported (0.619–0.629 acc), and the image encoder choice (ResNet50 vs ViT-L) shows only a small, ambiguous difference. Uncertainty: Whether a biologically-informed learned RNA encoder (scVI) meaningfully outperforms PCA in the multimodal setting is the largest untested design lever. This experiment (config_030: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) isolates the RNA encoder change within the best-supported multimodal architecture. If scVI improves over PCA, it opens a high-impact direction; if not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can redirect budget to fusion strategy or other variables. This is the highest-information experiment because the RNA encoder governs the representation of the dominant modality, and no evidence exists yet to guide that choice."
}

